Name: EasyList and EasyPrivacy filter lists
Short Name: filter_lists
URL: https://easylist.to/
Version: 202611071252 (EasyList), 202611071246 (EasyPrivacy)
Update Mechanism: Manual
License: GPL-3.0
License File: LICENSE
Shipped: yes
Security Critical: yes

Description:
EasyList and EasyPrivacy, the ad and tracker filter lists. The Filter Engine
(//components/aerie_adblock) compiles them into the engine that blocks requests
in the browser.

EasyList and EasyPrivacy are dual licensed: GPL-3.0-or-later, or CC BY-SA 3.0,
at the user's option (https://easylist.to/pages/licence.html). Aerie uses
them under the GPL-3.0-or-later option.

Local Modifications:
None. easylist.txt and easyprivacy.txt are the files that easylist.to served on
the dates of the versions above, committed byte for byte. filter_lists.lock.json
pins each by sha256 and size, and `./aerie build` fails if one differs.
`./aerie lists update` refreshes the files and the lock. aerie_adblock_compile
compiles them into a serialized engine at build time. Lines that are over 8 KiB,
or that are exception rules matching every URL, are dropped at compile time (see
components/aerie_adblock/rust/core/src/lib.rs).

-------------------- DEPENDENCY DIVIDER --------------------

Name: malware-filter phishing-filter (hosts)
Short Name: phishing_filter
URL: https://gitlab.com/malware-filter/phishing-filter
Version: 2026-11-08T00:02:34Z
Update Mechanism: Manual
License: CC-BY-SA-4.0
License File: LICENSE.phishing_filter
Shipped: yes
Security Critical: yes

Description:
malware-filter (curbengh) phishing-filter, "Phishing Hosts Blocklist"
(phishing-filter-hosts.txt). It lists phishing domains from OpenPhish, IPThreat
and PhishTank. Credit: malware-filter (curbengh), and its upstream feeds
OpenPhish (https://openphish.com/), IPThreat (https://ipthreat.net, CC BY-SA 4.0)
and PhishTank (https://phishtank.org/). The project is not endorsed by them, and
Aerie is not endorsed by the project. The Filter Engine's protection category
(//components/aerie_adblock) compiles the list into the engine that shows the
phishing and malware interstitial for a listed domain and its subdomains. The
list is CC BY-SA 4.0 (the project's code is CC0 and MIT). CC BY-SA 4.0 is
one-way compatible with the GPLv3, which is the licence of Aerie, so the
compiled engine can ship with it. The licence text and the credits are in
LICENSE.phishing_filter.

Local Modifications:
None. phishing_filter_hosts.txt is the file that
https://malware-filter.gitlab.io/malware-filter/phishing-filter-hosts.txt
served on the date in Version above, committed byte for byte. Version is the
list's own `# Updated:` time. protection_lists.lock.json pins it by sha256 and
size, and `./aerie build` fails if it differs. `./aerie lists update` refreshes
the file and the lock. aerie_protection_compile compiles it into a serialized
engine at build time (see components/aerie_adblock/rust/core/src/protection.rs).
The compiler skips lines that are not plain domain names.
